-- title:
--   Base change of a rational node ring to a larger constant layer
-- statement:
--   Fix a field $k$ of characteristic zero, a field extension $L/k$, a valuation subring $A \subseteq L$, a field extension $F/L$, and extensions $\overline{F}_1, \overline{F}_2$ of the residue field of $A$. Let $R_1, R_2$ be regular prolongations of $A$ to $F$ with values in $\overline{F}_1, \overline{F}_2$ (each given by a valuation subring `integers` of $F$ meeting $L$ exactly in $A$, together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto $\overline{F}_i$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and such that every nonzero element of $F$ has a nonzero residue after scaling by a constant), and let $x_1, x_2$ be places of $\overline{F}_1, \overline{F}_2$ over the residue field of $A$, with $\mathrm{ord}$ the associated order function. Let $S$ be a nonempty set of places $P$ of $F$ over $L$, each rational (the residue field of $P$ is generated by $L$), and let $\mathcal{N} \subseteq F$ be the subring of elements lying in $R_1.\mathrm{integers}$, in $R_2.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation subring of every $P \in S$; assume the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\, f \in L$ of every $f \in \mathcal{N}$ at every $P \in S$ lies in $A$. Let $K_0 \le K'$ be intermediate fields of $L/k$, finite over $k$, and let $C$, $C'$ be the subrings $A \cap K_0$ and $A \cap K'$ of $L$ (both contained in $A$), assumed to be discrete valuation rings, and let $\varpi' \in C'$ be such that an element $d \in C'$ has residue $0$ in the residue field of $A$ exactly when $d$ is a multiple of $\varpi'$. Let $\mathcal{N}_0 \subseteq \mathcal{N}$ be a Noetherian local subring such that: $S$ consists precisely of those places $P$ of $F/L$ whose valuation subring contains $\mathcal{N}_0$ and at which every non-unit of $\mathcal{N}_0$ takes a value lying in the maximal ideal of $A$; the image of $C$ in $F$ lies in $\mathcal{N}_0$; every $g \in \mathcal{N}_0$ differs from the image of some element of $C$ by a non-unit; any family in $L$ linearly independent over $C$ admits no nontrivial vanishing combination with coefficients in $\mathcal{N}_0$; and, for $i = 1, 2$, each $f \in \mathcal{N}_0$ lying in $R_i.\mathrm{integers}$ has $\mathrm{ord}_{x_i}$ of its $R_i$-residue non-negative, and strictly positive when $f$ is a non-unit with nonzero residue. Finally let $x, y \in \mathcal{N}_0$ with $x$ having $R_1$-residue $0$ and nonzero $R_2$-residue, and $y$ conversely. Then there exists a Noetherian local subring $\mathcal{N}_0'$ of $F$ with $\mathcal{N}_0 \le \mathcal{N}_0' \le \mathcal{N}$ such that: $S$ admits the same description in terms of $\mathcal{N}_0'$; the image of $C'$ lies in $\mathcal{N}_0'$; every $g \in \mathcal{N}_0'$ differs from the image of an element of $C'$ by a non-unit; families in $L$ linearly independent over $C'$ admit no nontrivial vanishing combination with coefficients in $\mathcal{N}_0'$; non-units of $\mathcal{N}_0$ stay non-units in $\mathcal{N}_0'$; if the image of $\varpi'$ lies in $\mathcal{N}_0'$ then the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{N}_0'$ is contained in the sum of the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{N}_0$ and the ideal generated by that image of $\varpi'$; the two regularity-and-positivity conditions at $x_1$, $x_2$ hold for $\mathcal{N}_0'$; the Krull dimension of $\mathcal{N}_0'$ is at least $2$; and the presentation as a localisation is preserved, in the sense that whenever $B_0 \le \mathcal{N}_0$ is a subring with $\mathcal{N}_0 = \{f : f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B_0$ with $h$ a unit of $\mathcal{N}_0\}$, the same description holds for $\mathcal{N}_0'$ with $B_0$ replaced by the subring generated by $B_0$ together with the image of $C'$ and units taken in $\mathcal{N}_0'$.
--
--   This is the base-change step in the construction of rational node rings along a tower of finite layers of constants: it enlarges a Noetherian local node ring defined over the layer $C = A \cap K_0$ to one defined over the larger layer $C' = A \cap K'$, preserving the description of the node places $S$, the linear disjointness from the constants, the regularity and positivity of the two branch reductions, dimension at least two, and the presentation of the ring as a localisation of a finitely generated subring. It is used by the statements producing layered rational node rings and node charts for modular curves at full level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_NodeAnnulusEngine_exists_localizedBaseChange_of_layer_pos_localization.lean

import Mathlib
